--- COORDINATED VULNERABILITY DISCLOSURE ---

We partner with Bugcrowd for our private, paid bug bounty program and to handle public Coordinated Vulnerability Disclosures (CVD).

For the most streamlined communication, and to ensure you can claim your ticket in Bugcrowd, please make sure you have a Bugcrowd account beforehand.

The paid bounty program is currently invite-only; you can earn an invitation and Bugcrowd points by responsibly disclosing a vulnerability to us.

For well-written CVD reports and high-impact findings, we may provide a monetary reward at our sole discretion.


--- SCOPE INFORMATION ---

Before submitting a report via email, please review the Scope section below to ensure your finding is applicable.

E-mail address (responsible disclosure only): aircall-esf@submit.bugcrowd.com

We require a structured report that specifically confirms scope alignment:

The Finding: Describe the vulnerability you discovered. 
Scope Alignment: Provide a specific, detailed explanation of why your finding falls within the defined In-Scope rules. 
Reference the relevant sections of the security.txt scope (e.g., "This targets the Aircall Public API under https://api.aircall.io/," or "This impacts business logic concerning user data, which is explicitly in scope.").

IN-SCOPE TARGETS:
We are looking for flaws ranging from application security to cloud security. Any issue that
could affect how we handle calls, messages, companies, users, and everything in between is in scope.
Note that a company administrator has extensive rights over their company and its assets.
Primary Targets:
- Aircall Public API and its inner workings (e.g., endpoints under https://api.aircall.io/).
- Aircall Internal APIs (e.g., phone.aircall.io, mobile.aircall.io, internal.aircall.io, workspace.aircall.io, and others).
- Aircall VoIP Servers, including Softswitch.
- Aircall Marketing website and developer documentation (aircall.io, developers.aircall.io, and all subdirectories).
- Administration dashboard (dashboard.aircall.io).
- Aircall apps (iOS, Android, web, Mac, and Windows clients).
- Other non-marketing applications under aircall.io (e.g., assets.aircall.io).
- Back-office interfaces for unauthenticated testing only (e.g., admin.aircall.io — focusing on break-ins, authentication bypass, or information exposure).

OUT OF SCOPE:
- Flood-based Denial of Service (DoS).
- The authenticated portions of our back-offices (except for authentication/bypass issues) — i.e., admin.aircall.io.
- Vulnerabilities related to CVEs published within the last week.
- Vulnerabilities found in third-party tools and integrations not hosted directly under .aircall.io.


